        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Popol Vuh</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1550 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Kʼicheʼ people, through oral tradition; a writer soon after the Spanish conquest, perhaps Diego Reynoso or Cristóbal Velasco, may have recorded it; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friar</a> Francisco Ximénez transcribed it and translated it into Spanish in the early 18th century</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">Narrative in the Kʼicheʼ language written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> letters, in parallel columns with Ximénez's Spanish translation; undivided in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a>, it is usually edited as a preamble and four books</span></div>
